HST Office: full-window File view ("Trang Tập tin", backstage).

- sfx2/source/backstage: BackstageWindow, a child of the frame's container window that covers its client area while the
  ribbon is hidden, created on first use and reused. Left column in the application colour (the ribbon tint darkened to a
  4.5:1 contrast with white), pages Home, New, Open, Info and Save As; the other items close the view and dispatch their
  command to the frame. The recent list reads SvtHistoryOptions, the Start Center's list and pinning.
- .uno:HSTBackstage is answered in SfxBaseController::queryDispatch instead of a new slot, because a change to sfx.sdi
  regenerates the slot headers of sw, sc and sd. Alt+F opens it (Global accelerators, not on macOS).
- The File tab: an application event listener sees TabpageDeactivate and TabpageActivate of notebookbar tab controls and,
  for the page "FileLabel", selects the previous tab again and opens the view. The wheel over the tab strip only skips it.
- The classic menu bar and its File menu are unchanged.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-backstage.py.
